### Synchronization — Laravel is authoritative; persist data.operation_id and data.server_id locally
POST {{baseUrl}}/sync/push
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{"operation_id":"{{$guid}}","device_id":"{{deviceId}}","entity":"account","action":"create","local_id":"{{$guid}}","payload":{"name":"Offline cash","type":"cash","currency_code":"ETB"},"client_occurred_at":"2026-08-16T10:00:00+03:00"}

### Incremental sync — on SYNC_CURSOR_EXPIRED, begin a full authoritative sync
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/pull?cursor={{syncCursor}}&limit=100
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Full resync — includes current archived resources, retained tombstones, and pending server-side states
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/pull?full=1&limit=100
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Recorded sync operation — only visible to its owner
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/operations/{{syncOperationId}}
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
